  finite-X equation after J=X J~: -Jtilde_response*X_response - X_response*chi_response*k_response**2 = 0
  exact X=0 equation before cancellation: 0 = 0  (chi arbitrary)
  X->0+ response: -1/k_response**2
  two paths with source gap -> 0 retain field gap -> -Delta_Jtilde/k_response**2
  [PASS] D9 (GATE 9) the zero-field limit is not controlled by this ansatz: at exact X=0 the lambda equation is 0=0 and selects no chi, while for every X>0 cancelling X gives chi=-J~/k^2.  Distinct J~ paths all approach the same (X,J)=(0,0) but retain distinct finite chi limits, so the solution map is path-dependent/nonunique   (Delta source -> 0; Delta chi -> -Delta_Jtilde/k_response**2)

